needed to prevent U-Boot's `1.5s` `InUsbBurn` window from aborting with `noSof / sof timeout`.\n2. **Why `update.exe bulkcmd \"setenv lock 10100000\"` Is Superior to `\"watchdog off\"` as the 48ms Probe:**\n   - Inspecting `update.exe` binary strings showed that if a U-Boot build does not implement a `watchdog` command, `update.exe bulkcmd \"watchdog off\"` returns `[update]ERR(L%d): AmlUsbBulkCmd failed!`. Using `\"setenv lock 10100000\"` as the `48 ms` probe uses a guaranteed standard U-Boot command (`setenv`) and unlocks `lock=10100000` in the very first USB packet.\n3. **Ghost `PID_0D02` USB Handle After Reboot:**\n   - When U-Boot executes `fastboot reboot` on a box with `otg_device=0`, Windows retains a stale `USB\\VID_18D1&PID_0D02\\Z41220090388172` PnP node. Pinging `fastboot getvar version-bootloader` with a `900 ms` timeout accurately distinguishes a live Fastboot session (`4–14 ms` response) from a ghost descriptor (`TIMEOUT`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **`FAILED (remote: 'locked device')` and false `[OK] Bootloader desbloqueado` in `media_1793771264706_95b71ed4.png`:**\n  - *Root cause:* The script did not check `getvar unlocked` output (`unlocked: no`) or test partition write before claiming unlock success, and dumped raw `fastboot oem` errors to stdout/stderr.\n  - *Fix:* Wrapped all tool calls in `InvokeToolSafe` (capturing stdout/stderr with timeouts), verified both `getvar unlocked` and a real write test on `_aml_dtb`, added `ReadChoiceWithKeepAlive` (sending `getvar version-bootloader` every 2s while waiting for user input), and added `StartDedicatedWorldCupHuntFromLockedFastboot`.\n- **Premature Monitor Exit on `[FASTBOOT_LOCKED_ASSIST]`:**\n  - *Root cause:* The initial monitor script (`task-432`) triggered wakeup as soon as `[FASTBOOT_LOCKED_ASSIST]` was logged (before the user pressed `1` or `2` inside that menu).\n  - *Fix:* Updated the active monitor loop (`task-440`) to only trigger early wakeup on completion/error events (`[WORLDCU